{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"digital signature digital signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","fileName":"Digital Signature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Digital Signature","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[.NET Cryptography and Access Control]] [[Applied Cryptography and PKI]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Cryptography and Access Control","Applied Cryptography and PKI","Nonrepudiation","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"digital signature digital signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","fileName":"Digital Signature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Digital Signature","heading":"Digital Signature","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A digital signature uses a private key to sign data and a corresponding public key to verify the result. Verification provides evidence that the signed content has not changed and that the signer possessed the private key.\n\nPractical signature APIs usually hash the message and apply an asymmetric algorithm such as RSA to the digest using a defined padding scheme. Trust in the signature still depends on securely associating the public key with the claimed identity.\n\nDigital signatures support [[Nonrepudiation]] by giving a recipient verifiable evidence that the holder of a private key signed particular content. The public key checks that evidence, while a certificate or other trusted association is still needed to connect the key to a claimed sender.","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Cryptography and Access Control","Applied Cryptography and PKI","Nonrepudiation","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"digital signature digital signature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Digital Signature.md","fileName":"Digital Signature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Digital Signature","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n\n[[cybersecurity.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":[".NET Cryptography and Access Control","Applied Cryptography and PKI","Nonrepudiation","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","cybersecurity.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}